    "observations": [
      {
        "area": "Directional parsing and budgets",
        "finding": "Outbound observer_request and inbound signed_observation/transport_failure have exact separate shapes. The parser requires exact bytes, applies request/frame/message bounds, rejects duplicate and unknown keys, invalid UTF-8, nonfinite constants and floating overflow, and validates canonical base64. Sequence requires exact int (excluding bool) in 1..4096. Signature length is only a 256/384/512-byte shape check. Original decoded message bytes are retained without reserialization."
      },
      {
        "area": "No authentication or acceptance",
        "finding": "SyntheticRelay fields are unauthenticated labels. Dummy signatures remain unverified. A parsed payload is an opaque dictionary, and staging exposes neither safe/accepted facts nor continuation authority. The diagnostic reports signature_verified, host_facts_validated, observation_accepted and operational authorities as false with admission BLOCKED."
      },
      {
        "area": "Challenge and repeated response handling",
        "finding": "The parsed Challenge must equal the outstanding Challenge, including schema and all token/sequence components. The parser fixes the schema. No sequence or checkpoint advancement exists. A further response after staging latches UNEXPECTED_ADDITIONAL_RESPONSE rather than renewing authority."
      },
      {
        "area": "Stop latch and local generation",
        "finding": "Failure clears the staged item and latches TERMINAL_STOP on the generation supplied to the explicit synthetic fixture. Wire schemas cannot select a generation or carry a broker command. A latched model returns itself for subsequent receive/transport_lost calls, preserving the first failure. This is a model state only, not actual OS stopping."
      }
